                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course aims to cultivate students' awareness of prioritizing prevention, instilling in them the professional responsibility to prevent diseases. It provides foundational knowledge in epidemiology and equips students with essential competencies in delivering preventive services, including health education and health promotion. Structured around the ecological health model, the course is divided into four main sections: "Introduction", "Principles and Methods of Epidemiology", "Clinical Preventive Services", "Community Public Health", and "Health System and Health Management". These parts respectively introduce the basic knowledge of epidemiology, how to implement individual targeted behavioral interventions in clinical settings for preventive services, environmental factors and intervention measures that affect population health in the community, and the functions and operational elements of the health system related to providing safe and effective health services.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
